{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20497",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 5.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Right, morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.21,
      "end_seconds": 10.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.84,
      "end_seconds": 28.3,
      "duration_seconds": 15.46,
      "text": "Hello, um, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help. Hmm, it's cramping tummy pain, doctor. He didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.33,
      "end_seconds": 30.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.86,
      "end_seconds": 35.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'd say a week, uh, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 36.54,
      "end_seconds": 40.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.21,
      "end_seconds": 46.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.84,
      "end_seconds": 49.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "yes, somewhere around that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.44,
      "end_seconds": 64.85,
      "duration_seconds": 14.41,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.93,
      "end_seconds": 72.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day about a six out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.34,
      "end_seconds": 81.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 81.17,
      "end_seconds": 88.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "Well, uh, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.9,
      "end_seconds": 93.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Okay, so I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.23,
      "end_seconds": 99.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "that's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.0,
      "end_seconds": 102.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "There's nausea as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.31,
      "end_seconds": 107.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.06,
      "end_seconds": 110.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.9,
      "end_seconds": 118.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "okay, any confusion, severe abdominal pain or blood in the stool at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.46,
      "end_seconds": 135.3,
      "duration_seconds": 15.84,
      "text": "No, no confusion, no severe abdominal pain, no blood in the stool. I was feeling dehydrated at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.87,
      "end_seconds": 140.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Right, have you had any vomiting blood or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.19,
      "end_seconds": 147.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "no vomiting blood or black stools, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.4,
      "end_seconds": 154.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.17,
      "end_seconds": 157.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.62,
      "end_seconds": 175.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay, do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.69,
      "end_seconds": 180.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.78,
      "end_seconds": 182.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.43,
      "end_seconds": 187.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.81,
      "end_seconds": 192.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.18,
      "end_seconds": 197.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.14,
      "end_seconds": 215.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.67,
      "end_seconds": 221.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke. My sister had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.33,
      "end_seconds": 225.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.77,
      "end_seconds": 231.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.62,
      "end_seconds": 233.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.2,
      "end_seconds": 262.4,
      "duration_seconds": 27.2,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for two years. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. I've had arthritis in my knees, yes. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I have COPD. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.73,
      "end_seconds": 275.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.84,
      "end_seconds": 279.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.05,
      "end_seconds": 284.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Right, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.58,
      "end_seconds": 288.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "no surgery, you know, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.37,
      "end_seconds": 296.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment? I ask cos it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 298.6,
      "end_seconds": 319.41,
      "duration_seconds": 20.81,
      "text": "Uh, it's telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day, doctor. It's naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day, doctor. Yeah, uh, he is on Tiotropium inhaler, once a day, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.67,
      "end_seconds": 324.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Right, since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 325.47,
      "end_seconds": 327.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "For about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.3,
      "end_seconds": 331.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.84,
      "end_seconds": 346.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Okay, nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.64,
      "end_seconds": 369.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "okay: heart rate 105, blood pressure 107 over 67, SpO2 98 percent on room air, temperature is 39.3 degrees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.14,
      "end_seconds": 375.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.86,
      "end_seconds": 378.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.4,
      "end_seconds": 396.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "Your mouth is a bit dry and and your tummy is soft with mild tenderness all over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.85,
      "end_seconds": 416.88,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards infective gastroenteritis, likely after recent travel. Food poisoning is also on my list. A parasitic infection is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.2,
      "end_seconds": 421.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "So, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.93,
      "end_seconds": 452.41,
      "duration_seconds": 29.48,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now infective gastroenteritis, likely after recent travel is my leading thought, not anything worse. I think blood tests makes sense here, for dehydration. We should do a stool test for diarrhoea. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. What I'm giving you is oral rehydration salts, 1 sachet, after each loose stool, for three days. That's for dehydration."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.53,
      "end_seconds": 472.42,
      "duration_seconds": 16.89,
      "text": "Small sips often are better than large drinks, and eat plain food as soon as you can. We'll catch up if it isn't better in three days. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 473.39,
      "end_seconds": 478.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Um, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 480.13,
      "end_seconds": 481.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
}